  "which_norm": "Primary for comparing widths: per-parameter RMS weight at t_fit (L2/sqrt(#params)). Total L2 of all parameters grows with sqrt(#params), i.e. about linearly in width, even when every parameter has the same typical size, so it is collinear with width by construction and a coefficient on it cannot be told apart from a width effect. The RMS removes that built-in dependence. Total L2 is reported as the plan's original measure. 'Only through norm' is refuted under total L2 and inconclusive under RMS (all f=0.4 runs); the `main_only` fits (26 runs, 5 widths) are unstable under both and not used."
